  "issue_title": "Add a block-production stats header (inter-block time, throughput, author decentralization) to the blocks index page",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`GET /api/v1/blocks/summary` computes block-production analytics \u2014 inter-block time distribution, extrinsic/event throughput, block-author decentralization (concentration over each author's block count), and the spec-version spread \u2014 live from the `blocks` D1 tier (`workers/request-handlers/entities.mjs:2957` `handleBlocksSummary`, shaped by `src/blocks-summary.mjs:97` `buildBlocksSummary`). It has zero UI touchpoint: `apps/ui/src/routes/blocks.index.tsx` lists raw blocks in a paginated table (`blocksQuery`) with no aggregate dashboard above it \u2014 no inter-block time, no throughput, no author-decentralization signal anywhere on the page.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a block-production stats header to the blocks index page (`/blocks`) that renders inter-block time (mean/p50/p90), throughput (mean extrinsics/events per block), and block-author decentralization (Nakamoto coefficient) as a compact tile row above the existing blocks table.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/blocks/summary`\n- Query function: **none exists.** Searched `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` for any function calling `/api/v1/blocks/summary` or referencing `blocks-summary` \u2014 there is no `blocksSummaryQuery` (or similarly named) export; the file only defines `blocksQuery` (`queries.ts:1535`), `blockQuery` (`:1551`), `blockExtrinsicsQuery` (`:1564`), and `blockEventsQuery` (`:1578`), none of which hit `/summary`. **This PR must add the typed query function** following the existing `queryOptions` + `apiFetch`/`fetchList` + normalize pattern used by those four sibling block queries (and dozens more in the file), **as well as** the UI wiring \u2014 both in one PR, since a data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n  - Response shape to normalize (from `buildBlocksSummary`, `src/blocks-summary.mjs:97-202`): `{ schema_version, block_count, first_block, last_block, first_observed_at, last_observed_at, block_time: { count, mean_ms, min_ms, max_ms, p50_ms, p90_ms } | null, throughput: { total_extrinsics, total_events, mean_extrinsics_per_block, mean_events_per_block, max_extrinsics_in_block } | null, distinct_authors, author_concentration: { holders, total, gini, hhi, hhi_normalized, nakamoto_coefficient, entropy, entropy_normalized, ...top-share fields } | null, distinct_spec_versions, latest_spec_version }`. `author_concentration` is the output of `computeConcentration()` (`src/concentration.mjs:165`) \u2014 the same scorecard shape already normalized elsewhere in `queries.ts` (e.g. `nakamoto_coefficient`/`gini`/`hhi_normalized` coercion at `queries.ts:1802-1814` and `:3430-3456` for other concentration surfaces), so follow that existing null-safe numeric-coercion convention rather than inventing a new one. A cold/empty store returns a schema-stable zeroed card (all the nested objects `null`, counts `0`) \u2014 never a 404 or throw.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File(s) to change:\n  - `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` \u2014 add `blocksSummaryQuery`, mirroring the shape/staleTime (`STALE_SHORT`, `queries.ts:143`) of the adjacent `blocksQuery` (`:1535`)\n  - `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` \u2014 add the corresponding `BlocksSummary` type (mirroring how sibling block types like `Block`/`BlockExtrinsics`/`BlockEvents` are defined)\n  - `apps/ui/src/routes/blocks.index.tsx` \u2014 the target page; confirmed current at 227 lines, `BlocksPage` component (line 48) renders `PageHero` then a `QueryErrorBoundary` + `Suspense`-wrapped `BlocksTable` (line 60), then `ApiSourceFooter` (line 63)\n- Exact anchor: insert the new stats-header block inside `BlocksPage` (`blocks.index.tsx:48-66`), between the `PageHero` (line 51-57) and the existing `QueryErrorBoundary`/`BlocksTable` (line 58-62) \u2014 its own `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary` pair, independent of `BlocksTable`'s, so a slow/failed summary never blocks the table from rendering. Also add `/api/v1/blocks/summary` to the `ApiSourceFooter` `paths` array (currently `[\"/api/v1/blocks\"]`, line 63) and `/metagraph/blocks/summary.json` to `artifacts`.\n- What to render: a `StatTile` grid (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/charts/stat-tile.tsx`), the same primitive already used for the sibling block-detail stats row in `apps/ui/src/routes/blocks.$ref.tsx:126-139` (`grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3`, three `StatTile`s with `icon`/`eyebrow`/`value`/`tone`). Populate:\n  - Inter-block time tile \u2014 `data.block_time?.mean_ms` (fall back to `p50_ms`) as the headline value, with `p90_ms` as the `hint`\n  - Throughput tile \u2014 `data.throughput?.mean_extrinsics_per_block` / `mean_events_per_block` (two tiles, or one tile with both in `hint`)\n  - Author decentralization tile \u2014 `data.author_concentration?.nakamoto_coefficient`, following the existing `nakamotoTone()` coloring convention from `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/concentration-panel.tsx` (lines ~83-85) so a low Nakamoto coefficient (concentrated authorship) reads as a warn/down tone, consistent with how that same metric is already colored elsewhere\n- Coordination note: **issue #3390** (\"Add a block-throughput sparkline header to the blocks index page\") targets the **same file** (`blocks.index.tsx`) with a **different, already-shipped data source** (`chainActivityQuery`'s `activity.days[].block_count`, per that issue's own body) rendered as a sparkline, not a stats tile row. The two headers are complementary, not duplicative \u2014 this issue's tiles are point-in-time aggregates from `/api/v1/blocks/summary` over the current window; #3390's is a time-series sparkline of daily block counts. Whichever PR lands second should visually stack below/beside the other's header rather than replace it, and a reviewer should expect two PRs touching adjacent lines near the top of `BlocksPage`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` or `apps/ui/src/components/` (not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`)\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` gains a `blocksSummaryQuery` export that calls `GET /api/v1/blocks/summary`\n- [ ] `blocks.index.tsx`'s `BlocksPage` imports and calls `blocksSummaryQuery` via `useSuspenseQuery` (or `useQuery` if independently loading), rendered inside its own `Suspense`/error boundary separate from `BlocksTable`\n- [ ] The rendered header shows at minimum: an inter-block-time value, a throughput (extrinsics or events per block) value, and the author-decentralization `nakamoto_coefficient` value \u2014 each via `StatTile`\n- [ ] `ApiSourceFooter` on the blocks index page lists `/api/v1/blocks/summary` (and `/metagraph/blocks/summary.json`) alongside the existing `/api/v1/blocks` entry\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states handled: a loading `Skeleton` while the summary query is pending, a schema-stable zeroed-card response (block_count: 0) renders tiles with dash/placeholder values rather than crashing, and a query error surfaces via the same `QueryErrorBoundary`/`ErrorState` convention already used in this file and in `blocks.$ref.tsx`\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not build the daily block-count sparkline \u2014 that is issue #3390's `chainActivityQuery`-based work, filed separately against the same file\n- Do not add filtering/drilldown UI on top of the stats header (e.g. clicking a tile to filter the table by author) \u2014 this issue is display-only\n- Do not modify `src/blocks-summary.mjs` or the `/api/v1/blocks/summary` backend response shape \u2014 the backend is already shipped and stable; this is a pure frontend wiring PR\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
